WEBVTT

00:05.463 --> 00:08.508
Our window confirmed
the existence of the Cursed Womb

00:08.591 --> 00:10.135
approximately three hours ago.

00:10.635 --> 00:13.304
When the evacuation rate reached 90%,

00:13.388 --> 00:16.558
we sealed off the facility
upon evaluation of the scene.

00:16.641 --> 00:20.937
Residents within a radius of 500 meters
have also been evacuated.

00:21.980 --> 00:23.940
I have a question, Mr. Ijichi.

00:24.023 --> 00:25.608
What is a "window"?

00:25.692 --> 00:30.697
A window is an authorized combat personnel
who can confirm curses by sight.

00:30.780 --> 00:32.949
However, they are not Jujutsu Sorcerers.

00:33.033 --> 00:34.617
Oh, I see.

00:34.701 --> 00:35.785
Allow me to continue.

00:36.745 --> 00:39.122
Inside Dorm 2 of this detention center,

00:39.205 --> 00:44.252
there are five prisoners left
with the Cursed Womb.

00:44.836 --> 00:47.547
If the Cursed Womb manages to mutate,

00:47.630 --> 00:51.426
we predict that it will transform
into a Special Grade Cursed Spirit.

00:51.509 --> 00:53.178
-Special Grade…
-Special Grade…

00:53.261 --> 00:58.016
Hey, I still don't really get
all this "Special Grade" stuff.

00:58.767 --> 00:59.642
Well then…

00:59.726 --> 01:02.437
Let me explain it
so that fools can understand.

01:02.979 --> 01:04.397
First, Grade 4 Curses.

01:04.481 --> 01:06.191
A wooden bat will suffice.

01:06.274 --> 01:09.319
Grade 3 Curses.
You're probably safe with a gun.

01:09.402 --> 01:11.780
Grade 2 Curses.
You'll barely make it with a shotgun.

01:11.863 --> 01:14.657
Grade 1 Curses. You won't feel safe
even with a military tank.

01:14.741 --> 01:16.659
And then we have the Special Grade Curses,

01:16.743 --> 01:20.038
which you'll probably require
rapid carpet bombing.

01:20.121 --> 01:21.498
That's very dangerous!

01:21.581 --> 01:25.877
Usually, they dispatch Jujutsu Sorcerers
with an equal level to the Cursed Spirit.

01:26.377 --> 01:28.963
In today's case,
it would have been someone like Mr. Gojo.

01:29.047 --> 01:30.173
I see.

01:30.256 --> 01:33.092
So where's Mr. Gojo?

01:33.176 --> 01:35.303
-He's on a business trip.
-What?

01:35.386 --> 01:37.305
In the first place, someone of his caliber

01:37.388 --> 01:39.724
wasn't supposed to be
wasting time in a high school.

01:39.808 --> 01:41.976
Don't expect me to bring souvenirs.

01:42.060 --> 01:46.147
Unfortunately, we're always
understaffed in this line of business.

01:46.648 --> 01:49.943
Sorcerers often have to manage tasks
way beyond their capabilities.

01:51.152 --> 01:55.281
However, this is an emergency case.

01:55.365 --> 01:57.367
"Fighting is strictly forbidden."

01:57.450 --> 01:59.911
If you encounter
a Special Grade Cursed Spirit,

01:59.994 --> 02:02.038
your only choices are to escape or to die.

02:03.873 --> 02:07.043
Please heed your fears.

02:07.627 --> 02:12.799
Don't forget that your mission
is to confirm and rescue any survivors.

02:12.882 --> 02:15.218
Excuse me, about Tadashi…

02:15.301 --> 02:17.762
You can't do this! Please stand back!

02:17.846 --> 02:18.847
Tadashi…

02:18.930 --> 02:21.516
Is my son, Tadashi, all right?

02:21.599 --> 02:24.978
-Calm down, it's dangerous here.
-Let go of me.

02:25.061 --> 02:27.647
-Please stand back!
-She’s one of the victims' guardians.

02:28.231 --> 02:29.691
Please go back.

02:29.774 --> 02:33.862
It is suspected that someone
has spread poison within the facility.

02:33.945 --> 02:37.448
No further information can be disclosed
for the time being.

02:37.532 --> 02:38.950
How could it be?

02:40.451 --> 02:42.579
Why?

02:42.662 --> 02:46.541
Why is this happening?

02:48.293 --> 02:50.295
Fushiguro. Kugisaki.

02:51.004 --> 02:52.338
Let's rescue them.

02:52.422 --> 02:53.965
Of course.

04:26.015 --> 04:27.600
DORM 2

04:30.520 --> 04:31.729
Please be careful.

04:33.523 --> 04:35.608
I'm putting up the Veil.

04:35.692 --> 04:38.194
"Emerge from darkness,
that which is darker than black."

04:38.278 --> 04:40.697
"Purify this impurity."

04:44.450 --> 04:45.368
What?

04:48.079 --> 04:49.872
It's turning into nighttime!

04:49.956 --> 04:51.040
That's the Veil.

04:51.124 --> 04:53.293
We're very close
to residential areas this time,

04:53.376 --> 04:55.920
so it's a barrier to conceal us
from the outside world.

04:56.004 --> 04:56.963
This is awesome!

04:57.046 --> 04:58.214
How ignorant.

04:59.549 --> 05:00.717
Divine Dogs.

05:05.680 --> 05:08.474
As soon as the curse approaches,
it will let us know.

05:08.558 --> 05:10.059
Oh, I see!

05:10.143 --> 05:13.563
What a good boy! We'll be counting on you.

05:16.899 --> 05:17.942
Let's go.

05:21.571 --> 05:22.405
Wait!

05:25.533 --> 05:27.452
What is that?

05:27.535 --> 05:30.163
What's going on?

05:30.246 --> 05:33.583
Isn't this supposed to be
a dormitory with two floors?

05:33.666 --> 05:36.919
Calm down! This is a duplex building!

05:37.003 --> 05:38.212
No, it's not.

05:38.880 --> 05:41.674
This is an Innate Domain
created by the curse.

05:42.175 --> 05:44.510
This is my first time seeing
a domain so huge.

05:45.303 --> 05:46.220
Where's the door?

05:46.304 --> 05:48.097
-What?
-What?

05:48.181 --> 05:50.058
The door has disappeared!

05:50.141 --> 05:53.352
-Why? Didn't we just enter from there?
-That's right!

05:53.436 --> 05:56.814
-Oh, no, what should we do?
-It will be fine.

05:56.898 --> 05:59.442
This dog can remember
the scent of the entrance.

05:59.525 --> 06:01.360
-Oh, my!
-Oh, my!

06:01.444 --> 06:03.571
Good boy! Let me feed you some jerky!

06:03.654 --> 06:05.990
Give me all the jerkies here!

06:06.074 --> 06:07.408
Come on! Be serious!

06:07.492 --> 06:10.203
-Fushiguro, you're so reliable!
-What?

06:10.286 --> 06:13.748
With your help, we can save the survivors
as well as ourselves!

06:16.834 --> 06:18.252
Let's move.

06:49.617 --> 06:50.910
How terrible…

06:50.993 --> 06:53.830
I guess it's safe to say
that there are three people.

06:55.832 --> 06:56.666
TADASHI OKAZAKI

06:58.417 --> 06:59.710
Tadashi…

06:59.794 --> 07:02.296
Is my son, Tadashi, all right?

07:03.297 --> 07:05.716
I'm taking this body back.

07:05.800 --> 07:07.051
What?

07:07.135 --> 07:08.803
He is that woman's son.

07:08.886 --> 07:09.929
But…

07:10.012 --> 07:11.556
His face is still recognizable.

07:11.639 --> 07:14.016
Telling her that he's dead
without showing the body…

07:14.100 --> 07:16.310
Of course, his mother couldn't accept it.

07:18.813 --> 07:21.441
We have to confirm the status
of the remaining two people,

07:21.524 --> 07:23.025
so leave that body here.

07:23.109 --> 07:26.863
You're kidding!
The path we came from disappeared!

07:26.946 --> 07:28.739
There's no chance of coming back later!

07:28.823 --> 07:32.368
I'm not saying we're coming back!
I'm saying we're leaving him here!

07:32.869 --> 07:35.246
I have no intention

07:35.329 --> 07:38.499
of bringing back a corpse of someone
I never intended to save!

07:39.000 --> 07:42.795
You didn't intend to save them?
What do you mean?

07:42.879 --> 07:44.797
This is a juvenile detention center.

07:44.881 --> 07:48.551
Jujutsu Sorcerers receives information
on the crime scene in advance.

07:49.886 --> 07:51.304
Tadashi Okazaki…

07:51.387 --> 07:53.097
He was driving without a license

07:53.181 --> 07:56.058
and hit a young girl
who was on her way home from school.

07:56.142 --> 07:58.644
And this is his second offense.

08:00.313 --> 08:05.776
You've always wanted to save civilians
and point them to the right death.

08:05.860 --> 08:10.740
But what if the person you saved
takes someone else's life later?

08:12.200 --> 08:14.994
Then why did you save me?

08:16.871 --> 08:19.957
Stop it already! Jeez!

08:20.041 --> 08:23.169
What are you two doing? Are you fools?

08:23.252 --> 08:26.005
Consider the time and occasion--

08:27.965 --> 08:29.634
Kugisaki?

08:29.717 --> 08:32.887
Impossible! Did the Divine Dog
not detect the scent of the curse?

08:36.182 --> 08:38.184
-Itadori!
-What?

08:38.267 --> 08:42.271
Run! We'll find Kugisaki later…

08:47.485 --> 08:48.986
There's no mistake.

08:49.070 --> 08:50.905
This is the Special Grade Cursed Spirit.

08:50.988 --> 08:52.365
I can't move.

08:52.448 --> 08:53.741
Move!

08:53.824 --> 08:56.744
Come on, move!

08:57.495 --> 08:59.330
Save others.

09:10.591 --> 09:12.093
Itadori…

09:14.595 --> 09:15.596
What?

09:19.850 --> 09:22.687
Goodness. Where am I?

09:22.770 --> 09:25.273
It's dark and I can't see anything.

09:27.316 --> 09:28.651
I can smell a curse!

09:30.236 --> 09:32.446
What's with the amount of curses?

09:37.201 --> 09:38.327
Nue!

09:48.713 --> 09:51.966
Please don't die, Itadori and Kugisaki!

09:52.842 --> 09:56.012
There's no escaping anymore
since I'm this close.

09:57.138 --> 10:00.891
Hey, Sukuna. You'll die if I die, right?

10:00.975 --> 10:02.935
Help me if you don't want that!

10:03.019 --> 10:04.395
I refuse.

10:04.478 --> 10:06.897
Even if I die in your body,

10:06.981 --> 10:10.401
I still have 18 souls left.

10:10.985 --> 10:16.073
But what makes me angry
is that I can't control this body.

10:16.157 --> 10:20.494
Feel free to swap if you want to, but…

10:21.162 --> 10:24.332
Instead of killing the Cursed Spirits,
I'll kill that kid first.

10:25.082 --> 10:26.375
Next, I'll kill that woman.

10:26.459 --> 10:30.087
She's full of spirit,
so I think I'll have fun with her.

10:30.171 --> 10:32.465
I won't let you do that.

10:32.548 --> 10:34.050
Guessed so.

10:34.133 --> 10:38.554
But if you keep talking to me,
your buddy's going to die.

10:45.519 --> 10:47.355
It's not using sorcery.

10:48.522 --> 10:51.400
It's just using cursed energy!

10:54.654 --> 10:57.156
Fushiguro!

10:57.823 --> 10:59.492
Fushiguro!

10:59.992 --> 11:02.411
Take Kugisaki out of here.

11:02.495 --> 11:06.040
I'll hold it down until you guys leave.

11:06.666 --> 11:09.251
After you're out,
find some way to send me a signal.

11:09.335 --> 11:10.628
After that…

11:11.754 --> 11:13.631
I'll change to Sukuna.

11:13.714 --> 11:15.424
It's impossible for you to win!

11:15.508 --> 11:17.551
How are you going to fight it
with bare hands?

11:17.635 --> 11:18.928
Look closely.

11:19.720 --> 11:23.891
He's enjoying it.
He's totally underestimating us.

11:23.974 --> 11:26.685
I can still buy time.

11:26.769 --> 11:27.853
You can't!

11:27.937 --> 11:29.313
Fushiguro.

11:30.648 --> 11:31.941
Please.

11:34.819 --> 11:36.695
Divine Dogs!

11:39.657 --> 11:41.283
Find Kugisaki!

11:44.787 --> 11:46.956
This is the last one.

11:49.125 --> 11:52.586
I should have brought a lot more.

12:01.512 --> 12:04.849
Is it easier to move around
in just your undergarment?

12:05.433 --> 12:06.642
But what should I do?

12:06.725 --> 12:09.687
I don't know
how to use cursed energy at all.

12:09.770 --> 12:12.481
Forget it. The important thing now
is to buy some time--

12:18.946 --> 12:21.824
What was that?
Some kind of cursed energy barrier?

13:02.323 --> 13:03.866
This seriously hurts.

13:03.949 --> 13:07.953
It feels terrible. Why would I…

13:08.037 --> 13:11.749
If I hadn't picked up the finger…

13:13.042 --> 13:14.168
If I hadn't eaten it…

13:14.752 --> 13:17.755
Back then…

13:17.838 --> 13:20.341
Stop! Don't think about it!

13:21.926 --> 13:23.219
No.

13:23.302 --> 13:25.387
I want to run away.

13:26.597 --> 13:27.681
I don't want to die.

13:29.517 --> 13:32.311
Even if I die here,

13:32.394 --> 13:34.730
is it considered a justified death?

13:38.484 --> 13:43.322
Stop thinking about it!

13:44.490 --> 13:46.242
Save others.

13:47.952 --> 13:49.203
Was I…

13:49.912 --> 13:52.122
really this weak?

13:55.209 --> 13:57.878
I remember your faces.

13:57.962 --> 14:00.381
I will curse you!

14:14.311 --> 14:16.105
We're getting out, Kugisaki!

14:16.188 --> 14:18.899
I hate frogs.

14:18.983 --> 14:20.109
Well, sorry about that!

14:27.908 --> 14:29.326
I overestimated myself.

14:30.494 --> 14:32.580
I thought I was strong.

14:33.372 --> 14:37.167
I thought I was strong enough
to choose my own death.

14:37.751 --> 14:39.253
But in reality, I'm not.

14:40.921 --> 14:43.424
I'm too weak!

14:44.675 --> 14:47.428
I'm just too weak.

14:49.763 --> 14:51.432
I don't want to die!

14:51.515 --> 14:55.185
I don't want to! But…

14:56.729 --> 14:58.272
I still have to die.

14:58.939 --> 15:02.484
It's not about having a justified death.

15:02.568 --> 15:04.028
Don't be naive!

15:04.653 --> 15:07.740
No Jujutsu Sorcerer
can die without remorse.

15:09.366 --> 15:14.038
Even so, you have to convince yourself
that it's justified.

15:15.497 --> 15:18.876
Curses emerge from the negative
emotions of human beings.

15:19.835 --> 15:21.629
If so, I'll use this hatred,

15:23.005 --> 15:24.465
fear,

15:25.132 --> 15:26.550
and regret.

15:27.051 --> 15:29.470
I'll release them all…

15:30.054 --> 15:32.556
into this fist of mine!

15:44.902 --> 15:47.154
Darn it.

15:51.033 --> 15:52.409
That howl…

15:57.247 --> 15:59.792
Was that Fushiguro's signal?

16:07.424 --> 16:10.803
This brat is really getting on my nerves.

16:14.515 --> 16:17.393
This brat is really getting on my nerves.

16:17.476 --> 16:20.854
He's totally looking down on me.

16:23.023 --> 16:25.818
Wait a minute. Let me think about it.

16:25.901 --> 16:29.738
I need to figure out a way
to make him regret it.

16:30.781 --> 16:32.074
Right.

16:32.157 --> 16:33.575
If I go after the other kid,

16:33.659 --> 16:36.328
he'll switch back
right before I get to him.

16:37.162 --> 16:42.543
That means "this" should
put him in a tough spot.

16:42.626 --> 16:44.753
I'll put you guys back to where you were.

16:45.295 --> 16:48.132
Hey. Let's go take down the kids.

16:48.716 --> 16:50.009
Follow me.

16:57.766 --> 16:58.934
You fool.

17:05.691 --> 17:08.986
Oh, no. I helped him heal his hand.

17:11.113 --> 17:12.698
You don't want to go for a walk?

17:13.449 --> 17:17.244
Well, Cursed Spirits usually
only loiter around their birthplaces.

17:17.327 --> 17:19.663
That's all good. If that's the case…

17:20.622 --> 17:23.709
Die here!

17:25.753 --> 17:27.588
Hey, what's wrong?

17:28.172 --> 17:30.257
This is not all you're capable of, right?

17:32.801 --> 17:36.805
That's right. Come on, you can do it!

17:41.685 --> 17:42.561
What?

17:45.522 --> 17:47.399
You might be a Cursed Spirit,

17:47.900 --> 17:50.277
but you still miss your limb?

18:07.044 --> 18:09.588
Please extend the evacuation zone
to ten kilometers.

18:09.671 --> 18:10.964
What will you do, Fushiguro?

18:11.548 --> 18:14.259
I'll be here waiting
for Itadori to come back.

18:14.343 --> 18:15.594
I see.

18:15.677 --> 18:18.931
I'll send Kugisaki to the hospital,

18:19.014 --> 18:21.183
and return here as soon as possible.

18:21.266 --> 18:22.392
It's fine.

18:22.476 --> 18:24.812
It's not like
you can do anything, Mr. Ijichi.

18:25.687 --> 18:30.609
If possible, please assign
a Grade 1 Jujutsu Sorcerer over here.

18:30.692 --> 18:32.986
Although, I don't think there's any.

18:33.070 --> 18:34.321
I'll try my best.

18:34.404 --> 18:35.614
I'm leaving.

18:43.664 --> 18:46.917
If something happens to him…

18:48.043 --> 18:49.670
I don't want him to die.

18:49.753 --> 18:52.256
It is personal.
Please do something about this.

18:53.924 --> 18:57.094
…I am obligated to deal with him.

18:59.721 --> 19:02.099
Hey, did you know?

19:02.182 --> 19:07.104
We're classified as
Special Grade Curse Spirits.

19:07.187 --> 19:10.274
Both you and I, I mean.

19:22.870 --> 19:24.830
Nice going, Special Grade Curse!

19:24.913 --> 19:26.290
Keep it up.

19:30.961 --> 19:32.546
You look happy.

19:32.629 --> 19:34.173
Shall I compliment you?

19:34.965 --> 19:38.218
But unlike humans,
it's not difficult for Cursed Spirits

19:38.302 --> 19:41.680
to regenerate with cursed energy.

19:42.931 --> 19:46.685
You and this brat…

19:47.352 --> 19:52.566
You guys really don't understand
anything about curses.

19:53.066 --> 19:55.611
This is a good opportunity.
Let me teach you…

19:56.320 --> 19:58.864
what real sorcery is.

20:01.366 --> 20:02.784
Domain Expansion.

20:11.501 --> 20:13.420
Malevolent Shrine.

20:20.052 --> 20:22.804
I wanted to cut you into three pieces.

20:22.888 --> 20:25.015
I guess you're really weak.

20:26.016 --> 20:29.144
Oh, yes, there's this too.

20:29.645 --> 20:31.563
I'm taking this with me.

20:41.365 --> 20:42.991
It's over.

20:46.536 --> 20:47.829
This is pissing me off.

20:47.913 --> 20:50.249
Just come out now
if you're going to switch places.

20:54.127 --> 20:56.171
What's wrong, brat?

22:35.937 --> 22:38.398
-Juju Stroll!
-Juju Stroll!

22:38.482 --> 22:40.901
Yes, I understand.

22:40.984 --> 22:43.403
Please take care of it. Yes.

22:43.487 --> 22:45.781
-Stare…
-Stare…

22:46.406 --> 22:47.407
What's wrong?

22:47.491 --> 22:49.910
So you bow
while talking on the phone, Mr. Ijichi.

22:51.203 --> 22:56.083
When I'm about to make a call,
I'll adjust my mood accordingly

22:56.166 --> 22:57.918
to make it an immersive experience.

22:58.001 --> 22:59.086
I can understand that.

22:59.169 --> 23:00.962
I've hurt my neck several times

23:01.046 --> 23:04.049
while trying to remove ingrown hair
during depilation.

23:04.132 --> 23:06.301
Of course, my pores were hurt too.

23:06.384 --> 23:07.928
Is that the same thing?

23:08.011 --> 23:11.556
Fushiguro gets agitated on the phone too.

23:11.640 --> 23:14.559
That's not about the phone call,
that's because it's Mr. Gojo.

23:14.643 --> 23:18.188
Itadori likes to walk around
while he's on the phone.

23:18.271 --> 23:19.606
Speaking of phone calls,

23:19.689 --> 23:21.900
can you guys sandwich
your phone on your shoulder

23:21.983 --> 23:23.693
while making a call?
